/** 
\mainpage %VW : Source-code documentation
The %VW project aims to provide a lightweight set of
classes and fast functions for performing basic computer-vision and
image-processing related tasks. This documentation has been built from the
source-code of the library and as such is quite technical in nature - for a more
gentle introduction to all things %VW see the user guide. Below is an index into
the library by functionality (section \ref Functionality), but first a list of
the individual libraries that make up the Workbench. (A search utility is
available <A HREF="search.html">here</A>.)


\section Libraries Libraries
%VW is split into several component
libraries of increasing dependance:
 
Core libraries
 
 - \link VNLPage VNL \endlink : A reduced version of the VXL project's numerics
library
 - \link VWCorePage VW \endlink: The core functionality (really should be called
VWCore). Image classes, image IO etc.

User interface libraries

 - \link VWXPage VWX \endlink: 2D user interface functionality using
raw X-windows commands.
 - \link VWXFormsPage VWXForms \endlink: 2D user interface functionality using
the XForms widget library.
 - \link VWGLPage VWGL \endlink: 3D user interface functionality using OpenGL
 - \link VWGTKPage VWGTK \endlink: 2D and 3D user interface functionality using
GTK--.
 - \link VWGLOWPage VWGLOW \endlink: 2D and 3D user interface functionality
using GLOW.
 - \link VWQtPage VWQt \endlink: 3D user interface functionality using Qt.
 
Hardware support

 - \link VWFirewirePage VWFirewire \endlink: Support for image capture
from IEEE1394 digital cameras
 - \link VWMeteorPage VWMeteor \endlink: Support for image capture from the
Matrox Meteor analogue capture card
 - \link VWYorickPage VWYorick \endlink: Control of the Yorick series of active
vision platforms
 - \link VWGTIPage VWGTI \endlink: Control of the GTI mobile robot


\section Functionality Functionality
Perhaps more usefully, the Workbench is indexed by category below. Classes that
provide related functionality are grouped by their function rather than by which
library they can be found in (although the two are often related).
 
 - \link Sequencers Sequencers \endlink :
Classes for retrieving images from a range of sources, including file lists,
movies, IEEE1394 cameras and the Matrix Meteor.
 - \link Image Image \endlink :
Image classes, IO and conversions.
 - \link ImageProcessing ImageProcessing \endlink :
Image filtering, mangling and feature detection.
 - \link GeometricObjects GeometricObjects \endlink :
Objects to represent geometric constructs such as points, lines, rotations,
multi-view relations etc.
 - \link GeometricAlgorithms GeometricAlgorithms \endlink :
Algorithms and operations on geometric objects, such as calculating
image-relations.
 - \link Displays Displays \endlink :
Classes for opening windows and drawing 2D things using a range of widget
libraries.
 - \link GLTools GLTools \endlink :
Classes that provide 3D OpenGL displays and 3D objects to draw on them.
 - \link UserInterface UserInterface \endlink :
Classes that provide widgets for controlling/viewing various VW objects.

*/
